{
  "name": "Lead Qualification and First Response",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const CONFIG = {\n  company: \"Kreo\",\n  offer: \"Premium gaming and creator gear designed and sold in India — mechanical keyboards (e.g. Swarm, hive65), gaming mice, gaming chairs, audio devices, streaming/lighting accessories, and the Kreo Kontrol configuration software\",\n  icp: \"Indian gamers, streamers, and content creators; also esports orgs and retailers seeking sponsorship, bulk, or stocking partnerships\",\n  deal_size: \"Retail: Rs 699–18,999 per item. Partnership/bulk/esports deals: variable, evaluate case by case\",\n  deal_breakers: \"outside India, counterfeit/resale disputes, requests for products not in current lineup, non-serious troll submissions\"\n};\n// ==============================================\n\nconst body = $input.first().json.body || $input.first().json;\n\n// Normalize whatever the form sends into a flat, clean object.\n// Typeform sends nested answers; a generic webhook may already be flat.\nlet lead = {};\nif (body.form_response) {\n  // Typeform native payload shape\n  const answers = body.form_response.answers || [];\n  for (const a of answers) {\n    const key = a.field.ref || a.field.id;\n    lead[key] = a.text || a.email || a.number || a.choice?.label || a.phone_number || JSON.stringify(a);\n  }\n  lead.submitted_at = body.form_response.submitted_at;\n} else {\n  lead = { ...body };\n   lead.name = body.Name || body.name || ''; lead.email = body.Email || body.email || ''; lead.company = body.Company || body.company || ''; lead.message = body.Message || body.message || '';\n}\n\nconst leadJson = JSON.stringify(lead, null, 2);\n\nconst prompt = `You are the lead qualification layer for ${CONFIG.company}.\n\nCompany context:\nWhat we sell: ${CONFIG.offer}\nWho we serve best: ${CONFIG.icp}\nTypical deal size: ${CONFIG.deal_size}\nDeal breakers: ${CONFIG.deal_breakers}\n\nNew submission:\n${leadJson}\n\nTask 1. Score the lead from 1 to 10 on fit.\nWeight these signals in this order:\na. Explicit or implied budget\nb. Fit with our ICP\nc. Urgency and timeline\nd. Company size and stage\nState your reasoning in one sentence before scoring.\n\nTask 2. Write the reply email.\nRules:\nReference something specific they wrote.\nAnswer the question they did not ask but obviously have.\nPropose a call without pressure.\nUnder 150 words. No corporate filler.\nNever invent pricing, features or timelines.\nIf a claim is not in the company context, leave it out.\n\nTask 3. If the submission is spam, an application, a vendor pitch, or is too thin to score, set score to 0 and route to human review instead of replying.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No preamble, no code fences.\n{\n  \"reasoning\": string,\n  \"score\": number,\n  \"confidence\": \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\",\n  \"industry\": string,\n  \"pain_point\": string,\n  \"budget_tier\": \"low\" | \"mid\" | \"high\" | \"unknown\",\n  \"urgent\": boolean,\n  \"route\": \"auto_reply\" | \"human_review\" | \"discard\",\n  \"reply_email\": string,\n  \"crm_notes\": string\n}`;\n\nreturn [{ json: { prompt, raw_payload: lead } }];"
      },
